<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech insurer Q1 97 gross profit rises.</title>
<headline>Czech insurer Q1 97 gross profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Republic's largest insurer, Ceska Pojistovna a.s., recorded a gross profit of 882 million crowns in the first quarter of 1997, up from 119 million in the first three months of 1996, according to filings with the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Unaudited results for three months ending March 31, 1997,</p>
<p>according to Czech accounting standards (in millions of</p>
<p>crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit	    881.65  vs	118.67</p>
<p>Net premiums from</p>
<p> life insurance	1,809.60  vs    1,806.07</p>
<p>Net premiums from</p>
<p> other insurance     4,627.94  vs    4,334.31</p>
<p> Total assets	 90,490.06  vs   78.707.38</p>
<p>NOTE: Pojistovna shares are traded on the main market of</p>
<p>the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
